      "order": 2,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "content": "> **Physical development:** Physical development is the way a child’s body grows and learns to move and use its muscles. It includes growth in height and weight, but it is much more than that.\n\n\n### Growth vs development\n\n| Concept | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Physical growth** | Physical growth means changes in the body’s size, such as becoming taller, heavier, or having larger muscles and bones. |\n| **Physical development** | Physical development means learning to control and use the body. This includes holding up the head, sitting, walking, running, holding a spoon, drawing, climbing, and balancing. |\n\n\n#### A simple example\n\n**Example:** A child may grow taller and gain weight, but physical development is also seen when the child learns to:\n\n- Sit without support\n- Crawl across the floor\n- Pick up a piece of food\n- Walk without holding an adult’s hand\n- Kick a ball\n- Feed themselves with a spoon\n- Turn the pages of a book\n\n\n> **Key Principle:** Physical development supports a child’s independence. When a child learns to walk, hold objects, dress, eat, and play, they can do more for themselves and take part more fully in family and community life.",
