      "content": "> **Gross motor skills:** Gross motor skills are movements that use the large muscles of the body. These include the arms, legs, back, and trunk—the middle part of the body.\n\n\nExamples include:\n\n- Holding the head up\n- Rolling over\n- Sitting\n- Crawling\n- Standing\n- Walking\n- Running\n- Jumping\n- Climbing\n- Balancing\n- Throwing and kicking a ball\n\n\nThese skills usually develop step by step. A baby first needs head control before sitting well. A child usually needs to walk before running confidently. However, children do not all follow exactly the same order or timing.\n\n\n**Example:** For example, one child may walk at 11 months, while another may walk at 15 months. Both can be developing well. What matters most is that the child is making steady progress over time.",
