      "title": "7. Nutrition, Sleep and Physical Development",
      "order": 7,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "content": "Nutrition, sleep, and general health work together to support physical development.\n\n\n- **Nutrition:** Nutrition provides energy for movement and nutrients for bones, muscles, and the brain.\n- **Sleep:** Sleep helps the body recover and supports growth, attention, mood, and learning.\n- **General health:** General health affects how well a child can play and learn. Repeated illness, untreated pain, poor vision, or ongoing feeding problems can affect a child’s activity and development.\n\n\n> **When to Seek Professional Advice:** A child who is well fed, rested, and healthy is usually more able to explore, play, and practise new skills. If a child is often tired, has poor appetite, is not growing as expected, or seems unusually weak or inactive, a qualified healthcare professional should assess the child.",
      "coachNotes": "Guide the student through nutrition, sleep and physical development, emphasizing evidence-based movement milestones, safe play, and early pediatric red flags."
