      "order": 9,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "content": "Children develop at different rates. Some walk early. Some talk early. Some become confident climbers later. Some children prefer watching before they try a new movement.\n\n\nThis variation is normal. A child should not be constantly compared with a sibling, cousin, neighbour’s child, or classmate.\n\n\n> **Important Note:** However, “children develop differently” should never be used to dismiss a real concern. A caregiver knows the child well. If a child is not progressing, has persistent difficulty with movement, or loses a skill they previously had, it is important to speak with a qualified healthcare professional.\n\n\n> **Clinical Evidence:** The CDC advises parents to act early if a child is not meeting milestones, has lost skills, or if the parent has any concern.",
