      "title": "13. Practical Activity",
      "order": 13,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "content": "### Practical Observation Activity: Observation activity: “Watch, Support, Encourage”\n\nChoose a child aged 0–5 whom you care for. Observe the child during normal, safe play for 10–15 minutes. Do not test, pressure, or diagnose the child.\n\n**Record the following:**\n\n- **How the child moves:** crawling, walking, running, climbing, balancing, jumping, or dancing.\n- **How the child uses their hands:** reaching, grasping, holding a spoon, turning pages, stacking, drawing, or picking up objects.\n- **What physical activities the child enjoys:** ball play, dancing, climbing, carrying objects, drawing, or outdoor play.\n- **What skills the child is practising:** balance, coordination, hand control, strength, or independence.\n- **How you can safely encourage more movement:** providing floor space, offering a ball, allowing safe climbing, encouraging self-feeding, or reducing long periods of sitting.\n\n**Follow-Up Action:**\n\nAfter the observation, write down one simple change you can make this week to give the child more safe opportunities to move and play.",
      "coachNotes": "Guide the student through practical activity, emphasizing evidence-based movement milestones, safe play, and early pediatric red flags."
