      "title": "14. Module 2 Key Takeaways & Comprehensive Assessment",
      "order": 14,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "content": "### Module 2 Key Takeaways & Summary\n\n1. **Physical development is more than getting taller and heavier; it includes learning to move and use the body.**\n\n2. **Physical growth refers to changes in body size, while physical development includes movement skills and coordination.**\n\n3. **Gross motor skills are large-body movements such as sitting, walking, running, jumping, and climbing.**\n\n4. **Fine motor skills are smaller hand-and-finger movements such as grasping, feeding, drawing, and turning pages.**\n\n5. **Developmental milestones are useful general guides, not exact deadlines.**\n\n6. **Children develop at different rates, and progress over time matters more than comparison with other children.**\n\n7. **Safe floor play, tummy time, active play, outdoor play, and everyday tasks support physical development.**\n\n8. **Good nutrition, adequate sleep, safety, and regular healthcare all support healthy development.**\n\n9. **Children do not need expensive toys; safe, simple, locally available materials can support play and learning.**\n\n10. **Persistent concerns, significant movement difficulties, or loss of previously learned skills should be discussed with a qualified healthcare professional.**\n\n### Professional Medical Note\nThis module provides educational information about physical development in early childhood. It does not diagnose developmental conditions or replace professional assessment.\n\nChildren develop at different rates, and a single difference from a milestone does not automatically mean something is wrong. However, parents and caregivers should seek advice from a qualified healthcare professional when they have ongoing concerns, notice significant movement difficulties, or observe a child losing skills they previously had. Urgent medical concerns should receive appropriate medical attention without delay.\n\n---\nTake the comprehensive 10-question Knowledge Check below to complete Module 2!",
